<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Les Formigues</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1285</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicilian-vespers">Sicilian Vespers</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Les Formigues was a naval battle fought in 1285 near the Formigues islets off the coast of Catalonia, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicilian-vespers">War of the Sicilian Vespers</a>. An Aragonese and Catalan fleet defeated a French fleet supporting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-iii-of-france">Philip III of France</a>'s invasion of Catalonia. The defeat threatened the French supply lines and contributed to Philip's retreat from the siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/girona">Girona</a>.</p></div>
